# Modern CSS Color Formats

```elixir
Mix.install([
  {:plotly_ex, "~> 0.3"},
  {:kino, "~> 0.18"}
])
```

## Hex alpha, space-separated RGB/HSL, and OKLCH

Plotly.js v4 accepts modern CSS color forms, including 8-digit hex with alpha,
space-separated `rgb()` and `hsl()` with slash alpha, and perceptual `oklch()`.
All four colors below include transparency, visible against the pale background.
This example uses a static Kino widget: it renders once, without live updates.

```elixir
alias Plotly.{Bar, Figure}

Figure.new()
|> Figure.add_trace(Bar.new(
  x: ["Hex alpha", "RGB / alpha", "OKLCH", "HSL / alpha"],
  y: [3, 4, 2, 5],
  marker: %{color: ["#3366CC80", "rgb(255 0 0 / 0.5)",
    "oklch(65% 0.2 145 / 0.7)", "hsl(270 80% 50% / 0.6)"]}
))
|> Figure.update_layout(title: "Modern CSS colors", plot_bgcolor: "#eeeeee")
|> Plotly.Kino.PlotlyStatic.new()
```
